### **Optimized Iterative Solution (Avoiding Recursion Overhead)**
Instead of using recursion (which repeats many calculations), use an **iterative approach** for better efficiency:
```c
#include <stdio.h>

int fibo(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return 0;
    if (n == 1) return 1;

    int a = 0, b = 1, sum;
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        sum = a + b;
        a = b;
        b = sum;
    }
    return sum;
}

